{
  "version": "0.9.1",
  "notes": "Added gps_test.py: a standalone Thonny bench test to check GPS signal live -- turns GPS on, polls AT+CGPSINFO with a 'still searching...' progress line every 5s (instead of gps.py's Gps.read() staying silent for its whole timeout), and reports a fix (lat/lon + clickable Google Maps link) or a clear 'no fix' with the most likely reasons (no dedicated GPS antenna -- a cellular-only antenna will NOT receive GPS, no clear sky view, or still mid cold-start). Does not touch cellular data (AT+CGPS/AT+CGPSINFO only), so it's safe to run standalone without opening a data session. Added Gps.read()'s new on_progress callback parameter (backward compatible, default None) to support this without changing read()'s behavior for existing callers.",
